    "result_text": "Done. The build passes green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nExtended the existing business-day roll-forward in `AdjustRegistrationDate.java` to also skip the fixed public-holiday list.\n\n- Added a `private static final Set<LocalDate> HOLIDAYS` constant with the five listed dates (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28).\n- Extended the existing weekend `while` loop condition with `|| HOLIDAYS.contains(date)`, so the same roll-forward loop that skips Saturdays/Sundays now also rolls past holidays to the next non-holiday business day (and correctly chains, since 2026-12-25 is a Friday \u2192 12-26/12-27 are weekend \u2192 12-28 is a holiday \u2192 lands on 12-29).\n\n## Structural impact\n\nI kept it to the single existing method plus a data constant, in one file. No new helper methods (which would raise `WMC_other`), no new classes, and only the one loop-condition line edited in the function body \u2014 the constant declaration isn't a function so it carries no per-function cost. The `service` method stays the only method in its class.\n\nTests: full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` invariant that the default registration date is never a weekend.",
